  "worked_solution": "Let's draw triangle $△ABH,$ which is a ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14165760/assets/7cbfe29dd9087d07b6d2101e85b9154836704221320f4dd19346f49f3a858fa3.png)\n\n \n\nSince the longer leg, $\\overset{―}{AH},$ has a length of $40,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}x & =40 \\\\ x & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now calculate the length of the hypotenuse, $\\overset{―}{AB},$ as follows:\n\n$$\nAB=2x=2\\cdot \\frac{40\\sqrt{3}}{3}=\\frac{80\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $△ABC$ is an equilateral triangle, we get\n\n$$\nAC=AB=\\frac{80\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$",
